{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/asyncthrowingstream\/init(unfolding:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@preconcurrency"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"unfolding"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"produce"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@escaping"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Scs7Elementxmfp","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Failure"},{"kind":"text","text":" == any "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Error","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A closure that asynchronously produces elements for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stream.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"produce"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this convenience initializer when you have an asynchronous function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that can produce elements for the stream, and don’t want to invoke","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a continuation manually. This initializer “unfolds” your closure into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a full-blown asynchronous stream. The created stream handles adherence to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol automatically. To terminate the stream with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an error, throw the error from your closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example shows an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncThrowingStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" created with this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"initializer that produces random numbers on a one-second interval. If the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random number is divisible by 5 with no remainder, the stream throws a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MyRandomNumberError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let stream = AsyncThrowingStream<Int, Error> {","    await Task.sleep(1 * 1_000_000_000)","    let random = Int.random(in: 1...10)","    if random % 5 == 0 {","        throw MyRandomNumberError()","    }","    return random","}","","\/\/ Call point:","do {","    for try await random in stream {","        print(random)","    }","} catch {","    print(error)","}"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncThrowingStream\/init(unfolding:)"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncThrowingStream"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Constructs an asynchronous throwing stream from a given element-producing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:Scs9unfoldingScsyxs5Error_pGxSgyYaKc_tcsAB_pRs_rlufc","modules":[{"name":"Swift","relatedModules":[]}],"title":"init(unfolding:)","symbolKind":"init","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"t